WEBVTT

1
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:26.124
TriedPath Fellowship presents:

2
00:00:26.144 --> 00:00:28.966
Understanding Your Roots.

3
00:00:29.116 --> 00:00:31.384
Part one. How your mind works.

4
00:00:31.404 --> 00:00:33.759
Our mind works like a computer.

5
00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:37.919
It is constantly placing
information into categories.

6
00:00:37.939 --> 00:00:41.425
If you feed something
destructive into your mind,

7
00:00:41.445 --> 00:00:45.962
it will add this to a stack of
similar material already there.

8
00:00:45.982 --> 00:00:49.371
As the stack grows larger, it
gains in power.

9
00:00:49.391 --> 00:00:52.625
In the computer industry, the
saying is:

10
00:00:52.645 --> 00:00:55.278
garbage in, garbage out.

11
00:00:55.298 --> 00:00:59.204
It is our responsibility to see
that the new information

12
00:00:59.224 --> 00:01:03.039
we receive is consistent with
our new life.

13
00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:06.338
>> New from TriedPath: Mountains
of Material!

14
00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:09.158
Scripture memory, on twelve
cassettes.

15
00:01:09.178 --> 00:01:12.374
In the car. In the kitchen. At
your bedside.

16
00:01:12.394 --> 00:01:13.839
Fill your memory tapes,

17
00:01:13.859 --> 00:01:15.651
and push the old material out!

18
00:01:15.671 --> 00:01:18.343
Operators are standing by!

19
00:01:19.293 --> 00:01:21.586
End of part one. Question two.

20
00:01:21.606 --> 00:01:25.981
Have you ever been able to stop
thinking about something?

21
00:01:26.001 --> 00:01:27.214
Did you succeed?

22
00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.414
Pause the tape, and write your
answer.

23
00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:37.890
Part two. Your roots.

24
00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.929
You were not born this way.

25
00:01:39.949 --> 00:01:42.346
It grew, one response at a time.

26
00:01:42.366 --> 00:01:46.036
And what was learned can be
unlearned.

27
00:01:46.636 --> 00:01:49.757
A child's security rests on
three bonds:

28
00:01:49.777 --> 00:01:52.348
mother to child, father to
child,

29
00:01:52.368 --> 00:01:54.097
and father to mother.

30
00:01:54.117 --> 00:01:57.807
Any break in this triangle
produces insecurity.

31
00:01:57.827 --> 00:01:59.702
Real, or only perceived,

32
00:01:59.722 --> 00:02:02.495
the results are the same.

33
00:02:04.295 --> 00:02:06.262
>> The TriedPath Pocket Library.

34
00:02:06.282 --> 00:02:07.900
Thirteen little booklets.

35
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.044
The roots, the way out, and help
for the family.

36
00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.414
Just one dollar each.

37
00:02:15.014 --> 00:02:18.889
Between two and six, a boy must
leave his mother's world,

38
00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:22.784
and his father must welcome him
into his own.

39
00:02:24.084 --> 00:02:26.905
But a boy with no welcome from
his father

40
00:02:26.925 --> 00:02:28.706
finds none among the boys.

41
00:02:28.726 --> 00:02:32.575
So he stays in the kitchen, with
his mother.

42
00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:35.993
>> Roots and Recovery. Now on
video.

43
00:02:36.013 --> 00:02:37.708
The developmental factors,

44
00:02:37.728 --> 00:02:39.439
and nine proven principles.

45
00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.462
Twenty dollars.

46
00:02:44.062 --> 00:02:47.103
He compares himself with other
boys.

47
00:02:47.123 --> 00:02:49.653
Comparison becomes admiration.

48
00:02:49.673 --> 00:02:52.049
Admiration slips into envy.

49
00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:56.123
At puberty, the envy becomes
eroticized.

50
00:02:56.623 --> 00:02:59.586
>> Un-Walk Steps. A weekly class
for men.

51
00:02:59.606 --> 00:03:01.556
Lessons read. Homework done.

52
00:03:01.576 --> 00:03:03.174
Pen and binder in hand.

53
00:03:03.194 --> 00:03:06.231
Keep a journal. And be on time.

54
00:03:07.631 --> 00:03:09.659
Part three. Displacement.

55
00:03:09.679 --> 00:03:11.726
Putting off, putting on.

56
00:03:11.746 --> 00:03:16.082
Displacement is the idea that
one thing pushes out another.

57
00:03:16.102 --> 00:03:18.176
There is no neutral ground.

58
00:03:18.196 --> 00:03:21.523
If there is a vacancy there,
evil will fill it.

59
00:03:21.543 --> 00:03:25.369
Interference is the technical
name for displacement.

60
00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:27.883
New material coming into your
mind

61
00:03:27.903 --> 00:03:30.054
pushes the old material out.

62
00:03:30.074 --> 00:03:32.996
In thirty days, we forget eighty
percent

63
00:03:33.016 --> 00:03:34.393
of what we learned.

64
00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:37.272
For you, that is a blessing.

65
00:03:37.872 --> 00:03:41.587
Turn on any radio or television,
and you will find

66
00:03:41.607 --> 00:03:45.497
a mind-boggling barrage of new
morality propaganda.

67
00:03:45.517 --> 00:03:49.940
Gays on television are shown as
superior people.

68
00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.425
What do we lose?

69
00:03:53.445 --> 00:03:57.259
The associations, triggered by
music, clothing,

70
00:03:57.279 --> 00:03:59.053
and many other things.

71
00:03:59.073 --> 00:04:02.634
Bars will close. The scene will
change.

72
00:04:02.654 --> 00:04:03.700
Question five.

73
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.345
What do you do when associations
from the past overwhelm you?

74
00:04:08.365 --> 00:04:12.058
Pause the tape, and write your
answer.

75
00:04:13.758 --> 00:04:16.825
So fill your memory tapes with
new material,

76
00:04:16.845 --> 00:04:20.051
until the bulk of it ejects the
old.

77
00:04:20.071 --> 00:04:23.563
We forget things that are
contrary to our opinions.

78
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:26.622
If we are ambivalent, the new
information

79
00:04:26.642 --> 00:04:29.680
will find no permanent home in
our minds.

80
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.335
This places the burden directly
on us.

81
00:04:34.135 --> 00:04:35.219
>> You may be saying:

82
00:04:35.239 --> 00:04:37.060
"I don't want to go to this
class!"

83
00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.508
Women Relating to Men.

84
00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:40.681
For all married and single
women.

85
00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.381
Thursday, at seven-thirty.

86
00:04:42.401 --> 00:04:45.883
Don't end up saying: "I wish I
had gone."

87
00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:48.192
For further study:

88
00:04:48.212 --> 00:04:51.578
booklet one, from our Pocket
Library.

89
00:04:51.598 --> 00:04:54.586
Homosexual people say they never
asked

90
00:04:54.606 --> 00:04:56.328
for their orientation.

91
00:04:56.348 --> 00:04:58.844
In most cases, that is true.

92
00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.522
Something they never chose.
